From: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qpycore_pyqtslot: don't use PyWeakref_GetObject()

PyWeakref_GetObject() was removed in Python 3.15.  Its replacement,
PyWeakref_GetRef(), is only part of the limited API from Python 3.13, but
PyQt5 is built with Py_LIMITED_API=0x030a0000.

Call the weak reference object instead, which works with every version.
The returned reference is still borrowed and Py_None is returned if the
referent has been destroyed, so callers are unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
AI-Generated: Uses Kiro (Claude Sonnet 5.5)
Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
---
--- a/qpy/QtCore/qpycore_pyqtslot.cpp
+++ b/qpy/QtCore/qpycore_pyqtslot.cpp
@@ -219,7 +219,21 @@
 {
     // Use the weak reference if possible.
     if (mself_wr)
-        return PyWeakref_GetObject(mself_wr);
+    {
+        // AI-generated: PyWeakref_GetObject() has been removed from Python
+        // 3.15 and PyWeakref_GetRef() is not part of the limited API before
+        // Python 3.13.  Calling the weak reference works with all versions.
+        // Like PyWeakref_GetObject() we return a borrowed reference, or
+        // Py_None if the referent has gone.
+        PyObject *obj = PyObject_CallNoArgs(mself_wr);
+        if (!obj)
+        {
+            PyErr_Clear();
+            return Py_None;
+        }
+        Py_DECREF(obj);
+        return obj;
+    }
 
     return mself;
 }
